WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.710
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.570
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.050
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.050
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.410
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.920
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.410
What?

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:27.870
It's Sonic!

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.210
It's Sonic!

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:36.050
Sonic!

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.380
No way!

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:44.950
Episode 43

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:44.950
Huge Home Electronics Panic!!

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:54.320
Good morning.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.730
Good morning.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:59.030
Can you please check these documents immediately?

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.490
Okay. Put them right here.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.620
Okay.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.460
What's with all these documents?

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:20.930
These are complaints that our home appliance department received over the weekend.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.720
Complaints?

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.260
That's ridiculous!

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.060
What's going on?

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:29.680
No one has ever complained about our products before.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.640
Please look at this.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:37.530
Sonic's deeds have made a great impact on the people.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:42.860
Groups of citizens are skipping school and work to attend Sonic appreciation events.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:45.700
Others sleep all day on their roofs.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.910
There's an increase in the number of people who go on vacations and don't come back.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.960
This is turning into a social phenomenon.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:58.090
They believe that Sonic's carefree lifestyle is cool and the situation is becoming serious.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:02.680
This is Scarlet Garcia reporting for SSTV.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:08.970
Sonic is very popular.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:14.350
But what does that have to do with the complaints?

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:17.730
Many of our employees are also Sonic fans.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.900
They're skipping work, so there are fewer workers in our factories.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:26.870
And the ones that are working do whatever they want, like Sonic. Therefore, the quality of our products go down.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.990
The result is this stack of complaints!

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.040
Please check these documents immediately and give us your orders.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.790
Okay! This is the job for the CEO!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.880
Hello?

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:46.220
What happened to Chris?

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:52.390
He's caught a cold and has a slight fever, so I'm keeping him home from school.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:55.140
There's no need to tell dad about this.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:05:00.780
If he drinks delicious hot chocolate and rests, he'll recover in no time.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:04.450
Please don't worry, sir. I'll handle it.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.450
But...

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.530
You never know what might happen, so I'm coming over right away!

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.160
Prepare the high-speed helicopter for takeoff immediately!

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.080
Is there a problem?

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:19.420
My son has a fever so high that it's keeping him from school!

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:25.090
Tell the person in charge to take care of the complaints with compassion. Got it?

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:26.380
President!

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:48.200
Who asked for a helicopter?

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:00.040
Dear, what are you doing?

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.960
Lindsay, big trouble! Chris has a cold!

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.300
What?

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:15.890
Oh, magnificent!

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:20.600
Okay, next.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:21.730
Okay.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.440
Okay, next.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:26.360
Okay.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:27.360
Okay, next.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.490
Okay.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:32.030
Okay, next.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:33.120
Okay.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:36.410
Okay, next.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:37.450
Okay.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:55.350
Dr. Eggman, you're working too fast!

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.850
I'm not broken!

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.810
Don't take me apart!

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:03.860
Why are you so hyper?

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:06.190
Take it easy.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.530
Don't you understand?

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:12.360
Look at the mountains of objects that need to be repaired!

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:15.580
This is all Sonic's fault.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:27.250
Look! Since Sonic became popular, many people copied his carefree personality and made shoddy products!

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:34.090
Therefore, all these appliances have come to this prison factory for repair!

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:37.390
Everything is Sonic's fault!

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:41.270
If it's Sonic's fault, let's stop making repairs.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:45.270
That's right. Let's leave them alone.

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:51.360
That's your opinion? And that's what greatly separates you from me, the genius Dr. Eggman!

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.530
There he goes again.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.070
It happens every time.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.740
Listen up.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:02.500
I'm going to get my revenge on Sonic by using this.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.000
Whoa! That's...

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:08.090
Just watch, Sonic!

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:17.350
Thank you.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.150
How's Chris doing, Ella?

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:32.110
He's fast asleep. I'm sure he'll get better quickly.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:33.030
I see.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:36.910
Ella, we've received the vacuum cleaner you sent for repairs.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.120
It's finally here.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:44.160
All the recent electrical appliances aren't very good, so they always break.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:45.920
I wonder why?

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.630
Ella, I'm sorry.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:54.340
I usually would've fixed it for you, but I've been busy working on Emerl.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:57.340
It's fine. Please don't worry about it.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:59.850
Is something wrong with Emerl?

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:06.940
When I analyzed its activity AI, all the data on its past was erased.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:11.820
Activity AI is the artificial intelligence that processes all actions.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:19.490
By analyzing it, we can find out what it did in the past and uncover Emerl's identity. However, that's not possible if the data has been deleted.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.370
I feel sorry for it.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:26.250
But it'll be fine because we're friends.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:30.710
You're very kind, Cream.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.020
Mom? Dad?

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.640
Are you all right, Chris? I was worried!

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:47.520
Same here!

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.480
Hey, Dad! Mom!

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:55.650
That's enough.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:58.240
More importantly, what about work?

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:01.870
After I heard Chris had a fever, I couldn't stop myself.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:03.200
Same here.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.500
You idiots!

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.790
Why don't you grow up?

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:12.420
We're taking care of him, but once you hear that your son catches a cold, you fly here by helicopter?

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:14.000
Get a hold of yourselves!

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.300
But Father...

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:17.220
No excuses!

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:20.640
You're setting a bad example for your child, my stupid son!

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:23.140
Stupid son?

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:28.140
I can say the same about you, Dad! You always ditched work so that you could play with the kids!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.900
Stop bringing up stories about the past!

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:35.400
This is why your company's products are getting many complaints!

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.610
These two topics are not related!

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.860
The complaints are due to employees who are Sonic fans-

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:42.120
You're going to blame everything on Sonic?

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.370
I didn't raise you like this!

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.830
Both of you, stop!

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:48.620
Chris...

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:50.830
Chris, I'm sorry.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:53.380
I was just worried about you.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:55.500
I hate you, Dad!

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:59.550
And Mom, Grandpa, everyone! Leave!

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.220
Chris...

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:38.550
Both of you, there's no need to get so worked up.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:41.300
I have a good idea.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:46.260
If I make Chris his favorite cherry pie, he'll be in a good mood again.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:48.770
Nice! That sounds like a great idea.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:51.480
Let's all make it together.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:01.610
Mrs. Thorndyke, shall we begin?

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:05.450
Yes. Do we have all the ingredients?

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:08.290
Oh, we're forgetting the cherries.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.130
It won't open.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:17.000
That's strange.

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:22.300
Look out!

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.850
What's happening?

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:48.780
Hey, why is the hand mixer attacking people?

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:51.620
Look out, Sonic!

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:55.080
Thank you, Amy.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.670
It doesn't give up.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:32.330
Sonic!

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:34.830
Chris, are you all right?

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.210
Huh?

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:43.050
Emerl, you're...

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.760
What about it?

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:48.390
It used your Spin Attack, Sonic.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:49.930
What?

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:54.890
You...

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:00.860
It's copying Sonic's techniques.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.170
Chris!

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.420
Chris, I'm glad you're okay.

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:24.880
What's going on?

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:27.720
We don't have the slightest idea.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:31.300
However, there's only one man who could've done this.

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:33.100
Dr. Eggman.

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:37.060
If it's him, the town would now be in chaos!

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:54.990
It'll be fine because we know that they're weak against water.

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:56.450
That's true.

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:06.050
They must've stopped the water supply system.

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:08.550
They beat us to it.

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:11.130
Sonic!

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:12.220
I'm going too!

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:13.350
Dear...

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:17.140
My company made the water supply system for this city.

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:20.940
Therefore, it's my duty to perform customer support!

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.770
That's my company's motto.

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:25.650
Go, Nelson!

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:29.610
Tails and Amy, can you please go with him in the X-Tornado?

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:30.740
Understood!

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:35.200
I'm going too.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:37.540
No! I won't let you go!

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:38.450
But...

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.290
You have a fever.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.670
And you're also soaked in water.

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:45.170
Ella, please bring some dry clothes for Chris!

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:46.460
Okay!

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:55.800
I did it!

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:58.470
I win again.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.770
Sorry, Dr. Eggman.

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:04.310
Just wait. I'm going to make you feel a world of pain.

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:08.400
I'm in pain.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.530
Dr. Eggman's prophecy came true!

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:12.740
I told you so.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:17.240
Sorry to keep you waiting, Dr. Eggman!

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:25.420
We should've escaped like this from the beginning.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:29.710
Shut up! Timing is important.

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:31.380
You just wait, Sonic!

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:34.050
You'll witness the hell of electrical appliance robots!

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.110
They're weak against water.

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:51.990
Collect lots of water and pour it on them.

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:54.240
Understood! Thank you, Sonic.

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:56.490
Go! Hurry up!

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:03.580
I understand. Those electrical appliance monsters are weak against water.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:06.580
I'll dispatch the firefighters right away!

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:07.710
Thanks!

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.050
Knuckles.

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:19.470
Sonic, what's happened to this city?

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:22.270
There's no point in just beating them up.

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:25.190
They're weak against water.

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:29.940
The firefighters will be here soon, so we have to fight them until they arrive.

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:36.110
Sonic, how do you like fighting against electrical appliance robots?

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:39.320
This will be the last time that I'll see you.

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:44.000
You'll be buried under a mountain of electrical appliances and die!

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:12.400
At this rate, we'll run out of water!

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:14.480
The fire hydrant's water pressure is decreasing.

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.900
What's wrong with the water department!

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.290
Leave this to me!

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:35.340
It's fixed!

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:36.420
It's no good.

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:43.850
Though the supply system is restored, the dam's gate system that draws the water isn't opening.

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:46.100
There's no way you can fix it?

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:48.640
Actually, there's one way.

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:50.480
This is Nelson.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:51.770
What is it?

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.690
The water department's system has been repaired.

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:59.070
However, the dam's gate system has been destroyed, so we can't supply water.

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:01.870
We need to open the gate immediately.

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.780
How do you do that?

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:09.910
Mom, I want to go too.

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:10.750
No.

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:14.710
But I want to battle alongside Dad!

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:16.960
I don't want to stay here and do nothing.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:22.220
Your fever seems to have gone down.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:27.100
However, I can't let you push yourself too hard, so I'm going with you. Okay?

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:28.770
Of course!

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:39.030
Well done!

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:42.740
However, you're nearing the end, Sonic!

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:45.990
You should give up and go to the afterlife.

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:51.210
Dr. Eggman, it seems you're really going to beat him this time.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:54.250
Sonic, Knuckles, goodbye!

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:57.500
But now I feel like I'm going to miss him.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.670
All right! Do it!

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:03.050
Knuckles, you better not run out of energy.

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:05.140
That's my line!

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:29.080
Since the gate system is destroyed, we have to open up this valve.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:31.710
We'll have to work together!

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:47.680
It's Dad!

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:55.730
Chris, I can't believe you're here.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:59.860
How can I do nothing when you're fighting?

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:01.940
Chris.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:03.950
Dear, let's do it.

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:05.410
All right.

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:34.390
We did it!

00:21:34.390 --> 00:21:35.310
Yes we did!

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:36.730
We did it!

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:39.810
We did it!

